# Angular Conventions (Angular 20, standalone, signals-first)

## Application structure

```
src/app/
  core/            # singleton services, interceptors, guards, app-wide models
    services/
    models/        # interfaces, types, enums
  shared/          # reusable, dumb building blocks (no business logic)
    components/    # button, card, section-title, ...
    directives/
    pipes/
  features/        # one folder per feature/page
    landing/
      landing.ts / .html / .scss        # page (smart) component
      components/                        # section components used only by this page
        hero/
        footer/
      landing.data.ts                    # static content/config for the page
```

- A component that is used by 2+ features moves to `shared/`.
- Feature pages are lazy-loaded via `loadComponent` in `app.routes.ts`.

## File naming (Angular 20 style — no type suffixes)

- Components: `hero.ts`, `hero.html`, `hero.scss` in a `hero/` folder. No `.component.*` suffix.
- Services: `property.service.ts` → class `PropertyService`. Pipes: `price.pipe.ts` → `PricePipe`. Directives: `scroll-reveal.directive.ts` → `ScrollRevealDirective`. Guards: `auth.guard.ts`.
- Selectors: `app-` prefix, kebab-case (`app-hero`). Directive selectors: camelCase with `app` prefix (`[appScrollReveal]`).
- Class names: PascalCase, named after what they are (`Hero`, `LandingPage` — no `Component` suffix for components, matching the CLI scaffold `App`).

## When to create things

- **New component** when: a template section exceeds ~80 lines, a block is repeated, a block has its own state/logic, or it is a self-contained visual section (hero, footer, card). Prefer many small dumb components + one smart page component.
- **New pipe** when the same value transformation appears in 2+ templates (e.g. currency/area formatting). Pipes must be pure and side-effect free.
- **New directive** when reusable behavior attaches to existing DOM (intersection-observer reveal, click-outside). Never for content — that's a component.
- **New service** when logic touches data/HTTP/state shared across components. Components never call HTTP directly.

## Components (TS)

- Standalone only (default in v20 — never set `standalone: true` explicitly, never create NgModules).
- `changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` on every component.
- Signals everywhere:
  - `signal()` / `computed()` for local state — no mutable class fields for template state.
  - `input()` / `input.required()` instead of `@Input()`, `output()` instead of `@Output()`, `model()` for two-way.
  - `viewChild()` / `contentChild()` signal queries instead of decorators.
  - `linkedSignal()` / `effect()` sparingly; prefer `computed()`.
- Use `inject()` instead of constructor injection.
- `protected` for members used only in the template; `readonly` for signals, inputs, outputs.
- Keep components thin: presentation + wiring only; logic goes to services or pure functions.
- Static content (nav links, feature lists, testimonials) lives in typed `*.data.ts` files or component `readonly` fields with interfaces from `models/` — never hardcoded repeatedly in templates.

## Templates (HTML)

- Native control flow only: `@if`, `@for` (always with `track`), `@switch`, `@defer`. Never `*ngIf`/`*ngFor`.
- Bindings: `[class.foo]`/`[style.width.px]` over `ngClass`/`ngStyle`.
- Use `@defer (on viewport)` for heavy below-the-fold sections.
- Semantic HTML (`header`, `section`, `nav`, `footer`, `button`), `alt` on images, `aria-*` where needed.
- Use `NgOptimizedImage` (`ngSrc`) for static images.
- No function calls in templates except signals and pure pipes.

## Styles (SCSS)

### Where styles live

- `src/styles.scss` — design tokens (`:root` custom properties), element resets, and the few global classes that must escape encapsulation (`.container`, `.section-panel`, `.reveal`, `.rich-text*` for `innerHTML` content, third-party overrides). Nothing else is global.
- `src/styles/_mixins.scss` — shared mixins only (`up()`, `hide-scrollbar`, `visually-hidden`); it must emit no CSS. Import with `@use 'mixins' as *;` (resolved via `stylePreprocessorOptions.includePaths`).
- Everything else is a component stylesheet. Encapsulation stays on (emulated); never `::ng-deep`, never `ViewEncapsulation.None`.

### Tokens

- Colors, fonts, radii, shadows, layout gutters, z-index layers and motion (`--transition`, `--ease-out`) are tokens in `src/styles.scss`; components only use `var(--...)`.
- No literal color values in components. Tinted transparency derives from a token: `color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-ink) 55%, transparent)`. Third-party brand colors are tokens too (`--color-whatsapp`, `--color-telegram`).
  - Allowed literals: `transparent`, `currentcolor`, and neutral white/black overlays `rgb(255 255 255 / a)` / `rgb(0 0 0 / a)`.
- `z-index` above 9 must be a layer token (`--z-header`, `--z-fab`). Values 1–9 are fine for stacking inside a component that sets `isolation: isolate` or `position: relative`.
- Units: `rem` for type, spacing and sizes; `px` only for hairlines (borders, outlines, underlines ≤ 3px), shadow offsets and blur radii. Layout with flex/grid, never floats or magic margins.

### File shape

Order inside every component stylesheet:

1. `@use 'mixins' as *;` (only if a mixin is used)
2. `@keyframes` declarations
3. `:host { display: ... }` — always present. Sections/cards use `block`; hosts that only render a top-layer or fixed element (dialog, FAB, progress bar) use `contents`; a host that must stretch as a grid/flex item declares that explicitly with a comment.
4. The block(s), one `.block { &__element {} &--modifier {} }` tree each, elements in DOM order.

### Selectors & nesting

- BEM-lite, kebab-case, one block per component (`.card`, `.card__title`, `.card--featured`). Modifiers and states nest under the element they change: `&--active`, `&:hover`, `&::after`, `.item--open &`.
- Parent-driven child state uses the double-`&` form inside the block: `&:hover &__image { ... }`. Never restate the block name outside its tree (`.card:hover .card__image` at root level).
- Max nesting depth 2 (block → element → state/pseudo). Flatten deeper chains with compound selectors (`&:hover::after`, `tbody tr:hover`) instead of nesting them.
- Prefer classes; bare element selectors (`img`, `svg`, `th`, `dd`) only for markup you don't control (tables, rich text, third-party) and only one level deep.
- Never style another component's selector or a global utility (`.container`) from a component; put a BEM class on the element instead (`<app-button-link class="agent__cta">`).
- `!important` is not used (the only exception is the global `prefers-reduced-motion` reset).

### Responsive & motion

- Mobile-first. Every breakpoint goes through `@include up(md | lg | xl)` (768 / 1024 / 1280px); no inline `@media (min-width: …px)` and no off-scale values. Feature queries like `(hover: none)` are written inline, nested under the rule they affect.
- Multi-value `transition`/`box-shadow`/`background` lists go one value per line. Prefer `translate`/`scale`/`rotate` properties over `transform` for animatable state.
- Everything that animates respects `prefers-reduced-motion` (the global reset covers transitions/animations; add a component rule only for state that must also change, e.g. hover `scale: 1`).

### Hygiene

- No hand-written vendor prefixes — the build autoprefixes. Sole exception: `display: -webkit-box; -webkit-box-orient; -webkit-line-clamp` for multi-line clamping.
- No dead selectors: if a template renames or removes a class/element, delete its rule. Two features needing the same block (FAB, form card, eyebrow) means a `shared/` component, not copy-pasted SCSS.
- Comments: `/* */` in component files (explain *why*, e.g. why a `:host` display or a UA-stylesheet workaround is needed); `//` in partials so nothing is emitted into consumers.
- Declaration grouping (not enforced by tooling, keep it readable): positioning → display/box model → borders/radius → background → typography → visual (`opacity`, `filter`, `cursor`) → motion (`transition`, `animation`).

## State & data

- Feature/app state: signal-based services (`signal` + `computed` exposed as `readonly`), not RxJS subjects.
- RxJS only at async boundaries (HTTP, router events); convert with `toSignal()` where consumed by templates.
- `httpResource()` / `resource()` for fetch-and-display data.

## SSR awareness

This app uses Angular SSR. Guard browser-only APIs (`window`, `document`, `IntersectionObserver`) with `afterNextRender()` or `isPlatformBrowser(inject(PLATFORM_ID))`.

## Quality bar

- Strict TypeScript: no `any`, explicit interfaces for all data shapes, `readonly` arrays for static data.
- After changes: code must pass `ng build` with no errors; fix all linter warnings you introduce.
